From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:51:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ec/lenovo/h8: Read no EC RAM in the battery _STA before _REG

AML must assume an operation region inaccessible until _REG
(RegionSpace, 1) is evaluated for it (ACPI 6.5, 6.5.4). The _STA of
BAT0 and BAT1 read the battery present bits from ERAM whenever the OS
evaluates them: macOS does so before its EC driver installs the
EmbeddedControl handler, and logs "No handler for Region [ERAM]" for
both at every boot, then evaluates them again later.

Keep ECAV in the EC device, set by _REG (3, Arg1), and have the _STA of
the batteries return 0x0F (no battery) while it is 0. Once the handler
is in, _REG notifies both batteries with 0x81, as a battery attach event
of the EC does, so that the OS checks them again. This is the pattern
of the System76 EC (ECOK). Linux installs the EC handler from the DSDT
and evaluates _REG in acpi_bus_init(), before acpi_scan_init()
evaluates the _STA of the devices, so nothing changes there.

An ECDT would let the OS reach the EC before the namespace is
enumerated, but it changes how every OS brings the EC up (Linux takes
its boot EC from it instead of the DSDT), and the methods would still
read ERAM before _REG.

TEST=Build the ThinkPad W541; in acpiexec on its DSDT, with _REG (3, 0)
the _STA of BAT0 and BAT1 return 0x0F without touching the EC region,
with _REG (3, 1) they read it again (0x1F with the battery present bit
set) and both batteries get Notify 0x81; the other battery, _PSR, HPET
and _PTS/_WAK checks of the earlier patches give the same results.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl |  8 ++++++++
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ec.asl      | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl
index 67b562dace..b06ee54412 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/battery.asl
@@ -427,6 +427,10 @@ Device (BAT0)
 
 	Method (_STA, 0, NotSerialized)
 	{
+		/* No ERAM before the EC driver of the OS: no battery yet */
+		If (!ECAV) {
+			Return (0x0f)
+		}
 		if (B0PR) {
 			Return (0x1f)
 		} else {
@@ -544,6 +548,10 @@ Device (BAT1)
 
 	Method (_STA, 0, NotSerialized)
 	{
+		/* No ERAM before the EC driver of the OS: no battery yet */
+		If (!ECAV) {
+			Return (0x0f)
+		}
 		if (B1PR) {
 			Return (0x1f)
 		} else {
diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ec.asl b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ec.asl
index 01737ab809..82b4c61a23 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ec.asl
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ec.asl
@@ -68,9 +68,21 @@ Device(EC)
 				DKR3, 1		/* Dock register 3 */
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * 1 while the OS has a handler for ERAM, from _REG (3, 1): until then
+	 * AML must not read ERAM (ACPI 6.5, 6.5.4). The _STA of the batteries
+	 * checks it, as an OS may evaluate them before its EC driver is up
+	 * (macOS: "No handler for Region [ERAM]").
+	 */
+	Name (ECAV, 0)
+
 	/* Called on OperationRegion driver changes */
 	Method (_REG, 2, NotSerialized)
 	{
+		If (Arg0 == 3) {
+			ECAV = Arg1
+		}
+
 		/* Wait for ERAM driver loaded */
 		if (Arg1 == 1) {
 			/* Fill HKEY defaults on first boot */
@@ -80,6 +92,12 @@ Device(EC)
 				^HKEY.INIT = 1
 			}
 		}
+
+		/* The batteries now read the EC: let the OS check them again */
+		If ((Arg0 == 3) && (Arg1 == 1)) {
+			Notify (BAT0, 0x81)
+			Notify (BAT1, 0x81)
+		}
 	}
 
 	Method (_CRS, 0, Serialized)
-- 
